{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C/C++ Header (.h)", "description": "This header file defines the interface for managing WiFi SSID objects within a TR-069 protocol implementation. It declares the class `hostIf_WiFi_SSID`, which provides methods to get and set various SSID attributes such as enable status, name, alias, BSSID, MAC address, and operational status, as well as managing hierarchical relationships like lower-layer interfaces. It also includes detailed documentation and licensing information.", "external_files": ["hostIf_main.h", "hostIf_utils.h", "hostIf_tr69ReqHandler.h", "hostIf_updateHandler.h", "Device_WiFi.h"], "external_methods": [], "published": ["hostIf_WiFi_SSID"], "classes": [{"name": "hostIf_WiFi_SSID", "description": "A class encapsulating the WiFi SSID interface, providing methods to manipulate and retrieve SSID properties, including enable status, name, alias, status, BSSID, MAC address, and related hierarchical interface attributes."}], "methods": [{"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_Enable", "description": "Retrieves whether the specified SSID is enabled or disabled."}, {"name": "set_Device_WiFi_SSID_Enable", "description": "Sets the enable or disable status of the SSID."}, {"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_Status", "description": "Fetches the current operational state of the SSID (e.g., Up, Down, Dormant, etc.)."}, {"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_Alias", "description": "Gets the alias of the SSID used for addressing."}, {"name": "set_Device_WiFi_SSID_Alias", "description": "Sets the alias for the SSID."}, {"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_Name", "description": "Retrieves the textual name assigned to the SSID."}, {"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_LastChange", "description": "Returns the seconds elapsed since the SSID entered its current operational state."}, {"name": "get_Device_WiFi_SSID_LowerLayers", "description": "Gets the list of interfaces stacked below this SSID."}, {"name": "set_Device_WiFi_SSID_LowerLayers", "description": "Sets the list of in